# Security Policy

## Reporting Security Issues

Security is an important part of the Codexeron ecosystem.

If you discover a potential security vulnerability, please report it responsibly.

Do not publicly disclose security issues before they have been reviewed and addressed.

---

# How to Report a Security Issue

When reporting a security issue, please include:

- Description of the vulnerability
- Affected project or component
- Steps to reproduce the issue
- Potential impact
- Additional technical details when available

Providing detailed information helps us investigate faster.

---

# Responsible Disclosure

We encourage responsible security research.

Please avoid:

- Accessing unauthorized data
- Disrupting services
- Testing against real user information
- Publicly sharing vulnerabilities before resolution

---

# Supported Versions

Security support depends on the project and release status.

Example:

| Version | Supported |
|---------|-----------|
| Latest Release | ✅ |
| Previous Releases | Depends on project status |
| Unsupported Versions | ❌ |

